# wikimill configuration — copy to `wikimill.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp wikimill.env.example wikimill.env
#
# `wikimill.env` is gitignored and must never be committed. This .example file
# is committed and must never contain a real value or secret.
#
# Precedence:  process environment  >  wikimill.env  >  built-in default.
# So a one-off override works without editing this file:
#   WIKIMILL_DUMPS_DIR=/mnt/ssd2/dumps ./bin/wikimill preflight
#
# `wikimill preflight` prints every resolved value, with secrets redacted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Launcher layer — read by bin/wikimill on the HOST, before Docker starts.
# These cannot be read from inside the container, because they decide how the
# container is built and what gets mounted into it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Docker invocation. Set to `docker` if your user is in the docker group.
#DOCKER_CMD=sudo docker

# Image tag the launcher builds and runs.
#WIKIMILL_IMAGE=wikimill:latest

# Force an image rebuild even when the cache is warm.
#WIKIMILL_REBUILD=1

# Print the docker command and exit without starting a container. Useful for
# checking exactly which host paths get mounted before committing to a run.
#WIKIMILL_DRY_RUN=1

# Where the Wikimedia dumps live on the HOST. Defaults to ./state/dumps.
# The three dumps total roughly 32 GB, so an external SSD or HDD is a normal
# choice. Mounted read-only into the container at /usr/src/app/state/dumps.
#
# NOTE: the SQLite database must NOT live on removable or non-POSIX media
# (exFAT/NTFS/USB) — WAL needs POSIX locking and a durable fsync. Only the
# dumps relocate; state/wikimill.db always stays on local disk.
#WIKIMILL_DUMPS_DIR=/mnt/external/wikimedia-dumps

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application layer — read by config.py INSIDE the container.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Public crawler identity. The Wikimedia User-Agent policy requires
# a descriptive agent with real contact information, and it is simply good
# manners toward every site we crawl. Requests are throttled or blocked
# without it. Put a URL or an email you actually monitor.
WIKIMILL_CONTACT=
WIKIMILL_USER_AGENT=wikimill/0.1.0 (+CONTACT)

# Comma-separated DNS resolvers. At least two are required: an `unregistered`
# verdict needs two independent resolvers to agree before it is believed.
#WIKIMILL_DNS_RESOLVERS=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8

# Global crawl concurrency. Per-registrable-domain concurrency is always 1 and
# is not configurable — that is a politeness guarantee, not a tuning knob.
#WIKIMILL_CONCURRENCY=8

# Default per-host delay in seconds when robots.txt declares no Crawl-delay.
#WIKIMILL_CRAWL_DELAY=1.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future credentials (none needed today — the loader and its redaction are
# already in place so adding one is a one-line change, never a retrofit).
# Any variable matching *_KEY / *_TOKEN / *_SECRET / *_PASSWORD is redacted
# everywhere wikimill prints configuration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#WIKIMILL_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN=
